{
  "_comment": [
    "Project aliases for the three environments created in Mission 6.4.",
    "ADR-047 makes the build flavor the environment selector on the app side;",
    "this is the same selection for the Firebase CLI, so a deploy names an",
    "environment rather than a project ID nobody can check at a glance.",
    "",
    "There is deliberately no 'default'. A deploy must say which environment it",
    "means: `firebase deploy --only firestore:rules -P dev`. The previous",
    "default pointed at vump-platform-f86af, which is exactly the shape of",
    "mistake that ships a rules change to the wrong project.",
    "",
    "vump-platform-f86af is still listed, because it is still live and still",
    "holds the four pre-split accounts. It is retired only once the new dev",
    "project is verified, and it is named 'legacy' so it cannot be reached by",
    "typing an environment name."
  ],
  "projects": {
    "dev": "vump-dev",
    "staging": "vump-staging",
    "prod": "vump-prod",
    "legacy": "vump-platform-f86af"
  }
}
